yaml/key
description: A scalar before the colon — plain or quoted
- >
  A key is a scalar — most often plain, quoted when it needs punctuation. (YAML also allows a
  whole structure as a key via the explicit `? ` form — rarely seen in practice.)
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  age: 1
  'first name': 2
  "tab\there": 3
